{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_7c2ed2e66e2f32740547a82738d59b67c1eb480e48bfa83adbb2c2b589b4aef3"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Design principles emphasize trust through transparency (visible agent activity, resource usage, git changes), status-driven color coding (blue mentoring, purple executing, amber paused, green finished), and refined glassmorphism aesthetics."}],"claim_ids":["clm_7c2ed2e66e2f32740547a82738d59b67c1eb480e48bfa83adbb2c2b589b4aef3"],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:19:47Z","created_by_operation":"op_167d8ec523564903bbeac6d27167d803","id":"pg_33ed5042ca9857ee9944fc54dba5d1fb","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/timwuhaotian-the-pair-impeccable-md-8d678875f777-fc54dba5d1fb.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_cf4720b26e1c50daa4331ef262497e62"],"title":"timwuhaotian/the-pair/.impeccable.md @ 8d678875f777","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:19:47Z","updated_by_operation":"op_167d8ec523564903bbeac6d27167d803"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:19:47Z","created_by_operation":"op_167d8ec523564903bbeac6d27167d803","id":"pg_7ea08132666e5eaf8f18390f59f2dffb","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/timwuhaotian-the-pair-readme-zh-md-8d678875f777-390f59f2dffb.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_9481fe1ee4cc50bea0aed15ebfec4225"],"title":"timwuhaotian/the-pair/README.zh.md @ 8d678875f777","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:19:47Z","updated_by_operation":"op_167d8ec523564903bbeac6d27167d803"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[],"claim_ids":[],"created_at":"2026-09-14T03:19:47Z","created_by_operation":"op_167d8ec523564903bbeac6d27167d803","id":"pg_895ed8df8e64529684f63df1af705942","maturity":"draft","page_type":"source","path":"pages/sources/timwuhaotian-the-pair-readme-ko-md-8d678875f777-3df1af705942.md","record_type":"page","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","source_ids":["src_2337ded3485b59458e5ad08f0d135d4b"],"title":"timwuhaotian/the-pair/README.ko.md @ 8d678875f777","updated_at":"2026-09-14T03:19:47Z","updated_by_operation":"op_167d8ec523564903bbeac6d27167d803"}
{"access":"public","aliases":[],"assertions":[{"claim_ids":["clm_1c670e34e6b9c69d0e2ee32123e7192ff5aec08d3d8dd7d05537f2c5bb8473ca"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Full automation mode operates with workspace-scoped permissions, and each pair stores its own runtime permissions under .pair/runtime/<pairId>/; global opencode permissions are not modified — permissions are session-specific."},{"claim_ids":["clm_253c50f7f0225a6bef01fb1103d26154a5cca98057d9ef0dd5fea2de3111677f"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The Pair is a free, open-source desktop app running two AI coding agents: a read-only Mentor that plans and reviews, and an Executor that writes code and runs commands, cross-checking each other's work."},{"claim_ids":["clm_31ef6244862bc709729aed83ece8c1b746bbd0c7a535af1539b829750d498e84"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The tech stack is Tauri 2.x with a Rust backend, React 19 + TypeScript frontend, Tailwind CSS v4, Zustand state, Framer Motion, and Lucide React icons."},{"claim_ids":["clm_4045cbc87953f2c5ec04e42aa6a9f0bd67fc7e1d34d20d43ae44827b13b42a77"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The agent workflow loops through Mentoring, Executing, and Reviewing stages, and runs are capped at a flat 20-iteration default, pausing for human review when the budget is reached."},{"claim_ids":["clm_44c3166fc8505eaa9932da57e432394649fb40b2a15c7cb52e50c9d164e5fdfc"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Session snapshots are saved automatically; on relaunch the app detects interrupted sessions and offers to restore them with full conversation history and turn state."},{"claim_ids":["clm_57fb6157afd3c0dbb4d46ad23f796ee4cea74f251cdd76496b2eb5ce90021b00"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The documented Rust backend includes PairManager (lifecycle), MessageBroker (state machine), ProcessSpawner (multi-provider), ContextBridge, QualityGate, SmartPause, Git Tracker, Worktrees, Session Snapshot, Resource Monitoring, Acceptance, and Report Generator modules."},{"claim_ids":["clm_75cf532ff4c887ec864560f8036d354d79a206bdcd580e93a910bc65d9d052c9"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Repository development practice: the README's Development section documents npm scripts for building and testing, including npm test for JS and Rust unit tests, typecheck, lint, e2e, and platform-specific build commands."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a0121c1ee5328eb5810974e4f291e190d8510fb5559d18b000a65336f0cd78b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Coordination features include structured handoff prompts, quality gates, smart-pause logic, and a per-turn step-cycle guard that kills runaway agent processes to prevent CPU exhaustion."},{"claim_ids":["clm_9a08c5d1988fd4fb42657cb85a7ccaceb55dcced7ae2070c3296b9eb07a53d94"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The app requires at least one AI provider CLI (opencode, Claude Code, Codex, Antigravity, or Kimi Code); Codex, Claude, Gemini, and Kimi are detected from installed CLIs and sign-in state."},{"claim_ids":["clm_d57c855cabaf32f9c107aaeded378a9909e258a1d3d4bc6ca20ee3e979ebd5c7"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"Besides the desktop app, a terminal CLI edition called Pair Code is available on npm (installable globally via npm install -g pair-code), sharing the same Mentor + Executor design."},{"claim_ids":["clm_e503dbd2ed75c7658f7ddf87c196fc2e6291cbd052a168000735f39a19ec893b"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"The product is model-agnostic: it can pair provider CLIs including opencode, Claude Code, OpenAI Codex, Gemini CLI, and Kimi Code in any combination, plus local models via Ollama."},{"claim_ids":["clm_f6b04680f526d06708e644c382a79f806d73e6abb428163f83346a458c70e5c6"],"opposing_claim_ids":[],"text":"No benchmark or agent-performance evaluation harness appears in the provided evidence; the only test-related material is the repository's own unit/e2e test scripts, so agent task performance appears unmeasured in this snapshot."}],"claim_ids":["clm_1c670e34e6b9c69d0e2ee32123e7192ff5aec08d3d8dd7d05537f2c5bb8473ca","clm_253c50f7f0225a6bef01fb1103d26154a5cca98